\end{align*}
Multiplying the first equation by 3 and the second equation by 2, we get:
\begin{align*}
6e + 9t &= 7.50 \\
6e + 4t &= 5.40
\end{align*}
Subtracting the second equation from the first, we get:
\begin{align*}
(6e + 9t) - (6e + 4t) &= 7.50 - 5.40 \\
5t &= 2.10 \\
t &= 0.42
\end{align*}
Substituting this value of $t$ back into the first equation, we can solve for $e$:
\begin{align*}
2e + 3(0.42) &= 2.50 \\
2e + 1.26 &= 2.50 \\
2e &= 1.24 \\
e &= 0.62
\end{align*}
